# LINE ENDINGS ARE DECIDED HERE, NOT BY EACH MACHINE'S core.autocrlf.
# The repository stores LF, and every checkout writes LF, on Windows and on the Mac alike. Without
# this file the Windows checkout wrote CRLF, the move to the Mac carried those files over, and git
# then reported 49 files as modified that differed only in line endings.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts: cmd.exe needs CRLF in the working tree. Stored as LF like everything else.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Never converted. text=auto detects binaries by a NUL in the first 8,000 bytes; these are declared
# so a file that happens to have none is not rewritten.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.lnk binary
